    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), plus the `AcceptanceBase`/`AuditLogCapture` helpers, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nOn successful owner creation, the endpoint now emits an audit line via the `AUDIT` logger containing the owner id, customerCode, and registrationDate.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New function class** `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 logs via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`:\n   ```\n   Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-14\n   ```\n   It takes the created `Owner` via `@Val` and runs after `SaveOwner`, so the generated `id` is populated. `LocalDate.toString()` yields ISO `yyyy-MM-dd`, matching Jackson's JSON serialization the test asserts against.\n\n2. **Wired into** `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, carrying the same `govern: [ transaction ]` governance as its neighbors, per the project's OfficeFloor conventions (one small function class per step, composed with `next:`).\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` test confirms the AUDIT line contains all three values (id, customerCode, registrationDate).",
